  "notes": "A dark app shell frames a white, paper-like printable OPL sheet, like a print preview that you edit in place. The sheet uses safety-signage conventions: a red lockout/tagout block with a padlock icon, numbered black step squares, and an amber dashed common-mistake note. Photos carry numbered yellow callout pills (1 Lock nut, 2 Height gauge, 3 Reads 142.5 mm) that link to the matching numbered mark badges on the steps; these are instructional callouts, not discussion pins. The comment card includes a system suggestion pulled from a related library sheet (OPL-L3-0377) with a unit-adjusted rewrite and a one-click Use this wording and resolve, which is not AI. The top bar has a changeover countdown (13:30 changeover · 6 h 06 min left) and a clock. The hidden Review tab holds a read-through agreement checklist for 8 people and a pre-sign-off gate (3 things left before sign-off). Large 48px touch targets suit a shop-floor tablet. The footer says changes are kept in this browser tab."
